On Sat, 15 Nov 2008 11:52:06 +0100, Friedrich wrote:

> Mark Healey wrote:
>> This is really a question about the patch program but I'll need it to
>> apply some patches so I'm asking here.
>> 
>> I installed the source RPM for fedora 8.  It had the tarball and some
>> patches.  I extracted the tarball and tried
>> 
>> ]patch nethack-3.4.3-config.patch
>> 
>> and got nothing, not even disk thrashing, until I CTRL-Ced out of it.
>> 
>> What am I doing wrong?
>> 
>> 
> extract the patches into the nethackdir and run:
> patch < nethack-3.4.3-config.patch
> or
> patch -p1 < nethack-3.4.3-config.patch -p1 ignores the first part of the
> path in the patchfile

Thanks.  It turns out that I needed to specify "-p0".  I thought that was 
the default, but the default is really "-p[all of them]".

Watch the headers for my next question.




